From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: tyn <tyn@localhost>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 06:48:00 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] tyn: sg-pc movie flags 1851 / 2492 (Game.exe PlayMovie
 0x460d00)

Game.exe PlayMovie sets flag 0x73b (1851) while a movie plays and stores the
cancel argument in 0x9bc (2492). The common table has SF_MOVIEPLAY 1823 and
SF_MOVIEFL 2493. MACROSYS2 label 375 (world line change) waits in a loop on
1851; with the common value the loop ended at once and MovieMain_Stop cut
every world line movie after its first frames.

TYN only (sg-pc profile data).

Verified on MuMu (Android 15 x86_64 emulator, not a real device), Steam data
with the 2018 Chinese patch: SG00_01 line 854, imv005 then imv007 play to the
end and the scene goes on.

diff --git a/profiles/sg-pc/scriptvars.lua b/profiles/sg-pc/scriptvars.lua
index e87b7ffc430d67f6ac371cfcf11afa1210a061c9..0d383c77440f0fbf09bdab26ac12da4387d3d768 100644
--- a/profiles/sg-pc/scriptvars.lua
+++ b/profiles/sg-pc/scriptvars.lua
@@ -22,6 +22,12 @@ sv.SW_MESMODE0 = 4363;
 
 sv.SF_SYSTEMMENUCAPTURE=1378;
 
+-- Movie flags of Game.exe PlayMovie (0x460d00): it sets flag 0x73b (1851) while a movie plays and stores the
+-- cancel argument in 0x9bc (2492); the common table has 1823 / 2493. MACROSYS2 (world line change, label 375)
+-- loops on 1851 until the movie ends, so with the common value it stopped every movie on its first frame.
+sv.SF_MOVIEPLAY = 1851;
+sv.SF_MOVIEFL = 2492;
+
 -- The common table puts SW_MESWIN0TYPE at 4422, which is the second mask priority in STEINS;GATE (the scripts write 34 / 100
 -- there). The scripts never set a window type, so read an unused block instead (draw window and text).
 sv.SW_MESWIN0TYPE = 7970;
